# Code style

## TypeScript

- Strict mode — no `any`
- Explicit types at service boundaries
- Models in `models/` — not inline in components

## Imports

```typescript
import { X } from 'src/modules/WorkforceActivity/...';
import { Y } from 'src/components';
```

Never use `@/` alias.

## Naming

| Artifact | Convention |
|----------|------------|
| Components | PascalCase `ActivityTimeline.tsx` |
| Hooks | `useX.ts` |
| Services | `ActivityXService.ts` static methods |
| Models | `x.model.ts` |
| SCSS modules | `ComponentName.module.scss` |
| Constants | `SCREAMING_SNAKE` |

## React

- `import * as React from 'react'`
- Named exports (not default) for components
- `'use client'` on interactive modules
- Business logic in hooks/services — not components

## Files

- Small, focused files
- Barrel exports in `index.ts` per folder
- Comments only for non-obvious business rules
